From: William Macready <william.macready@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:05:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] proto(s2a-p2b): fixture 9 (axis in the form but not read)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 leanncd/test/Semantics/SourceOracleAffineTest.lean | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/leanncd/test/Semantics/SourceOracleAffineTest.lean b/leanncd/test/Semantics/SourceOracleAffineTest.lean
index 1955ec01..56343b00 100644
--- a/leanncd/test/Semantics/SourceOracleAffineTest.lean
+++ b/leanncd/test/Semantics/SourceOracleAffineTest.lean
@@ -160,4 +160,12 @@ private def writeOrigin : SourceOrigin :=
 -- accept-neighbour: the in-range image `[a]` runs.
 #guard (tampered [(0, [(1, 7)])]).map (·.toOption.isSome) == some true
 
+/-! 9. an axis in the write form but not read: `Y[a+b] := X[a]`, `|k| = 6`. `b` occurs only on
+the LHS, so the occurrence box is (a, b) and each `X[i]` is written once per `j`.
+Hand, cell s = sum of X[i] over i with 0 <= s - i <= 2 (i in 0..3):
+s0 = 1; s1 = 1 + 2 = 3; s2 = 1 + 2 + 3 = 6; s3 = 2 + 3 + 4 = 9; s4 = 3 + 4 = 7; s5 = 4.
+Occurrences (12, ordered by (a, b)): X[i] repeated for j = 0, 1, 2. -/
+#guard parity (snap 6 [k] [.assign "Y" [.affine (.affine 0 [(1, a), (1, b)])] readX])
+  [1, 3, 6, 9, 7, 4] [1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4, 4, 4]
+
 end SourceOracleAffineTest
